    "done_when": "The independent review of jtmm-wall-from-coil-vv found imas_ambix/data/selene_deck.py's contour parse accepts decks it would mis-slice, and that the plan's claim that the coil_vv skins change representation and not geometry is asserted, never measured. In /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/coil_vv_OP1.dat (header line 446) and coil_vv_OP2.dat (header line 424) the contour block is a bare count 128 followed by rows 'R1 Z1 R2 Z2 index', with a label comment on the first row of each run: '%%Inner VV=50, ...', '%%Outer VV=50, ...', then seven '%%D-probe#N, ...' runs of 4 rows each. (1) _find_contour_header accepts a bare-count line only when the next numeric row carries a recognised run label; otherwise it keeps searching, and it raises ValueError when no such header exists. (2) _parse_contour_block raises ValueError, naming the deck line, when: a counted row precedes the first label; a label is not Inner VV, Outer VV or D-probe; an Inner VV or Outer VV run holds a different number of rows than its label's '=N' declares; either skin is empty; or a skin's chords do not join end to start within 1e-4 m, or its last chord does not end at its first chord's start within 1e-4 m. The skins it returns from both real decks are unchanged, so the store is not re-converted and nothing under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description is written. (3) tests/data/test_selene_deck.py feeds one synthetic deck per refusal case and asserts the ValueError. It also adds a geometry test reading both real decks and /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/EQSLE.DATA through parse_eqsle_deck: every vertex of each coil_vv skin lies within 1e-3 m of the matching EQSLE.DATA skin (inner to skin_inner, outer to skin_outer), measuring the distance to the nearest segment, with arcs measured as arcs. If any measured distance exceeds 1e-3 m, stop with status blocked and report the measured distances rather than loosening the tolerance, because the plan's representation-only claim would then be false. This session runs inside the fleet SLURM allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID is set), so the gate runs in place: TMPDIR=/tmp UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 tests/data/test_selene_deck.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py > <your log> 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?, exiting 0, with the gate log written under the run directory and its first line naming the revision, the tree and the command. UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-contour-parse-hardening.html records, per phase and skin, the vertex count and the maximum and median vertex distance to the EQSLE.DATA skin. The JT-60SA server is never contacted (no ssh jt-60sa, no EDDB call).",
    "estimated_hours": 1.0,
